  "caption": "Dark cinematic pop, 134 bpm, D minor, half-time feel in the verses and full time in the chorus. The ensemble: a sparse dripping piano figure in a huge, wet reverb; deep tom hits and a tight kick; a lean, round bass kept under the mids; a low string drone that swells into the chorus; soft plucked harp answering the piano. A low, hushed female lead in the reverb, stacked voices on the chorus. Mood: hushed and huge, a cathedral of enamel. Arc: piano alone, drums in at verse one, the chorus opening wide, a bridge with drums out, the final chorus lifted with stacked voices. D minor throughout, no harsh highs.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro: dripping piano in a huge reverb]\n\n[Verse 1]\nI'm the enamel and the curve\nI held a whole kid an hour ago\nnow the level drops a finger at a time\nand a ring is all I've got to show\nthe duck is parked against the tap end\nthe whale is sulking on her side\nthe crayons wrote a word along my wall\nand nobody read it, nobody tried\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe door goes to, the voices go\nand the toys stand up in the shallow blue\n\n[Chorus]\nBath time is over\nthe water is going\nthe toys are not\nthe toys are not\n\n[Verse 2]\nA kit box tipped beside the tap end\nand out they climb, unpainted, dry\nthey've never touched a drop of anything\nnot paint, not water, not a dye\nthey walk my floor in single file\nround the puddles, past the foam\nand the toys that floated here all evening\nplant their feet like this is home\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe door goes to, the voices go\nand the toys stand up in the shallow blue\n\n[Chorus]\nBath time is over\nthe water is going\nthe toys are not\nthe toys are not\n\n[Bridge: drums out, voice in the reverb]\nPull the plug, we'll still be here\ndrain me dry, we'll still be here\n\n[Final Chorus: lifted, stacked voices]\nBath time is over\nthe water is going\nthe toys are not\nthe toys are not\n\n[Outro: piano alone]\nThe toys are not.",
